O! while along the stream of Time, thy Name
Expanded flies, and gathers all its fame,
Say, shall my little Bark attendant fail, 380
Pursue the Triumph, and partake the Gale?
And shall this Verse to future age pretend
Thou wert my Guide, Philosopher, and Friend? 385
That urg'd by thee, I turn'd the tuneful Art
From Sounds to Things, from Fancy to the Heart;
For Wit's false Mirror held up Nature's Light;
Shew'd erring Pride Whatever Is, is Right;
That Reason, Passion, answer one great Aim; 390
That true Self-love and Social are the same;
That Virtue only makes our Blifs below;
And all our Knowledge is, Ourselves to know.
